{%- comment -%}
  Cancellations, Returns & Refunds Policy (V3).

  Source: FSS_Return_Policy_REVISED_v3_2026-08-30.md, approved by Tim in the
  canonical Gmail thread "Return Policy Revised - Please Implement - Based on
  #49046 Core Health Return Issue".

  NOT LIVE. The policy dated December 1, 2025 on /pages/return-policy remains
  controlling until Tim sends the PUBLISHED go-live notice. Before that notice:
  set "Effective date" below, and do not point the live return-policy page at
  this section.

  The INTERNAL ONLY open-items section of the source document is deliberately
  omitted and must never be rendered.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% style %}
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
    padding-top: {{ section.settings.padding_top }}px;
    padding-bottom: {{ section.settings.padding_bottom }}px;
  }

  .return-policy { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .return-policy h2 { margin: 3.2rem 0 1.2rem; }
  .return-policy h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .return-policy p, .return-policy li { line-height: 1.6; }
  .return-policy ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 2.4rem; }
  .return-policy li { margin-bottom: .8rem; }

  .return-policy .effective-date { font-weight: 700; }
  .return-policy .effective-date--unset { color: #d83d0e; }

  .return-policy .summary-box,
  .return-policy .example-box,
  .return-policy .contact-info {
    border: 1px solid #e5e5e5;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 2.4rem;
    margin: 2.4rem 0;
    background: #fafafa;
  }
  .return-policy .summary-box { border-left: 4px solid #d83d0e; }
  .return-policy .summary-box h3,
  .return-policy .example-box p:first-child,
  .return-policy .contact-info h3 { margin-top: 0; }

  .return-policy__editor-note {
    border: 2px dashed #d83d0e;
    color: #d83d0e;
    padding: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div class="page-width return-policy">
  {%- if request.design_mode and section.settings.effective_date == blank -%}
    <div class="return-policy__editor-note">
      Editor only: no effective date is set. This policy must not be published
      until an effective date is entered and Tim has issued the go-live notice.
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p><strong>TJF Ventures LLC d/b/a Fitness Superstore</strong></p>

  {%- if section.settings.effective_date != blank -%}
    <p class="effective-date">Effective Date: {{ section.settings.effective_date }}</p>
  {%- else -%}
    <p class="effective-date effective-date--unset">Effective Date: [TO BE SET AT PUBLICATION]</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <p>
    This policy applies to orders placed on or after the Effective Date above. An
    order placed before that date is governed by the return policy and
    product-specific disclosures presented when the order was placed, except where
    applicable law requires otherwise.
  </p>

  <div class="summary-box">
    <h3>SUMMARY</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Only new French Fitness and new Body-Solid products may qualify for a voluntary return</strong> (a change of mind, not a defect). Eligibility isn't automatic &mdash; the product must not be marked final sale, custom, special order, clearance, &ldquo;as is,&rdquo; or otherwise excluded, and all conditions below must be met.</li>
      <li><strong>Every other brand we carry &mdash; including all Core Health &amp; Fitness-supplied products &mdash; is final sale for voluntary returns</strong>, along with remanufactured, used, and open-box equipment of any brand. This applies even if the product works perfectly and you simply decide it's not right for your space.</li>
      <li>To request a return, contact us in writing within <strong>14 calendar days after delivery</strong> for a Return Authorization (RA). Nothing may be shipped, tendered to a carrier, delivered to a return location, disassembled, or professionally removed before a written RA is issued.</li>
      <li>An approved return must be tendered to the carrier within <strong>10 calendar days</strong> of the RA.</li>
      <li>Approved returns carry a <strong>25% restocking fee</strong>, plus actual outbound and return freight &mdash; deducted even if your order showed free/included/$0 shipping &mdash; plus any nonrefundable completed delivery/installation/service charges.</li>
      <li>The customer is responsible for all return-side deinstallation, extraction, repackaging, loading, insurance, and return freight, and for returning the product complete, clean, and in like-new resalable condition with original packaging.</li>
      <li><strong>A freight-damage claim, a defect, an incorrect item, or an incomplete shipment is not a voluntary return.</strong> The 14-day request window and 25% restocking fee don't apply to those &mdash; see &ldquo;Problems with your order&rdquo; below. Applicable freight-reporting, warranty, and legal timelines still govern those instead.</li>
      <li>Warranty and field-service work may be coordinated through <strong>National Gym Service LLC</strong>, our affiliated service coordinator. All return requests and claims go to Fitness Superstore, and Fitness Superstore issues any approved refund.</li>
      <li>Nothing in this policy limits any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be waived.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>What qualifies for a voluntary return?</h2>
  <p>A voluntary return is one requested because you changed your mind or are dissatisfied for a non-defect reason &mdash; personal preference, comfort, fit, foot-platform size, ceiling height, available space, access limitations, or deciding a different product would be better.</p>
  <p><strong>Only new French Fitness and new Body-Solid products</strong> may qualify, and only when every condition in this policy is met &mdash; timely written request, RA issued, condition and completeness requirements met, packaging intact or an approved replacement-packaging plan, and shipped within the 10-day window. A product-specific disclosure shown on the product page, cart, checkout, quote, invoice, or order confirmation before purchase can make an otherwise-eligible product ineligible; a written order-specific exception applies only to the order it was issued for.</p>
  <p><strong>Every other brand we carry &mdash; including all Core Health &amp; Fitness-supplied products</strong> &mdash; is final sale for voluntary returns, whether or not it has been installed. So is any <strong>remanufactured, used, or open-box</strong> item of any brand: these are serviced under warranty rather than returned for buyer's remorse, comfort, noise, size, or minor cosmetic reasons. Minor cosmetic characteristics on remanufactured equipment (scratches, touch-up paint, finish variation) are normal and not grounds for return; if you believe transit damage occurred, contact us within 7 days of delivery with photos.</p>
  <p>Before ordering, please independently confirm ceiling height, room dimensions, doorway/path clearance, and site access &mdash; our team can share available specs, but final-sale status isn't affected by fit or space issues discovered after delivery. None of this limits any warranty right or other right that cannot lawfully be waived.</p>
  <p>To request a return for an eligible product: contact us in writing within 14 days of delivery with proof of purchase, order number, delivery date, reason, current photos, and confirmation all parts/manuals/hardware/consoles/cables/keys are present. Approved refunds go to the original payment method or financing provider, less applicable deductions &mdash; we don't offer an automatic equal exchange or store credit; switching products requires an approved return plus a new order.</p>

  <h2>Problems with your order (not a voluntary return)</h2>
  <p>Freight damage, a defect, an incorrect item, or an incomplete shipment are handled under the applicable warranty, damage, or order-correction process &mdash; not the return terms above, and not subject to the 14-day window or restocking fee.</p>
  <p><strong>Freight damage:</strong> Inspect before signing. Note visible/suspected damage on the delivery receipt (e.g., &ldquo;possible concealed damage,&rdquo; &ldquo;crate punctured&rdquo;), photograph everything before unpacking, keep all packaging, and report to us within 48 hours when reasonably possible. Don't refuse delivery unless it's unsafe or substantially destroyed, or we/the carrier instruct otherwise &mdash; accepting with documented damage lets us pursue the carrier claim. Undocumented damage can weaken a carrier claim, though it doesn't eliminate rights that can't be waived.</p>
  <p><strong>Defects:</strong> Stop using the product if continued use may be unsafe. Contact us at <a href="mailto:sales@fitnesssuperstore.com">sales@fitnesssuperstore.com</a> or <a href="tel:+19252152927">+1-925-215-2927</a> with order number, serial number, photos/video, and diagnostic details. Allow reasonable service access and return requested parts when a prepaid process is provided. Warranty service may be coordinated through National Gym Service LLC, our affiliated service coordinator, which may arrange qualified third-party providers &mdash; but claims should be submitted to Fitness Superstore.</p>
  <p><strong>Wrong item / incomplete shipment:</strong> Contact us before installing or extensively using the product, with the order number, packing list, labels, serial number, and photos of everything received plus what's missing or wrong.</p>
  <p>In all three cases: we'll diagnose first and coordinate the applicable remedy &mdash; repair, replacement parts, on-site service, manufacturer support, replacement, refund, or another remedy required by the applicable warranty and law. Nothing here limits an implied warranty, express warranty, or other right that cannot lawfully be waived.</p>

  <h2>Costs and deductions on an approved return</h2>
  <p>A <strong>25% restocking fee</strong> applies, calculated on the product price paid after discounts (excluding tax and completed service charges). In addition, you're responsible for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Actual outbound shipping/freight (including split shipments and separately shipped consoles/components) &mdash; deducted even if the order showed free, included, or $0 shipping;</li>
    <li>Return shipping, freight, and insurance;</li>
    <li>Return-side deinstallation, disassembly, extraction, movement, professional repackaging, palletization/crating, loading, and accessorial costs;</li>
    <li>Any nonrefundable completed delivery, room-of-choice, assembly, installation, stair-carry, debris-removal, storage, or redelivery charge; and</li>
    <li>Documented deductions for missing components, damage, or other loss in value found at inspection.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you pay an approved carrier or service provider directly, that amount isn't deducted again. If Fitness Superstore arranges or advances a return service, packaging, pickup, or freight charge, the actual cost is deducted from your refund. Fitness Superstore isn't responsible for loss or damage during a customer-arranged return shipment &mdash; use a qualified carrier with adequate declared-value coverage.</p>

  <div class="example-box">
    <p><strong>Example only &mdash; actual costs vary:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Product price paid: $2,000 | Completed installation (separately paid): $300</li>
      <li>25% restocking fee: $500 | Outbound freight: $200 | Return removal/repackaging: $150 | Return freight: $250</li>
      <li><strong>Estimated refund if Fitness Superstore advances return-side costs: $900</strong> ($2,300 paid &minus; $300 installation &minus; $500 restocking &minus; $200 outbound freight &minus; $150 return service &minus; $250 return freight)</li>
      <li><strong>If you pay the return provider/carrier directly, those amounts aren't deducted again.</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Excludes any separate tax adjustment, inspection deduction, or financing-provider adjustment.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Condition, packaging, and installed equipment</h2>
  <p>An approved return must be complete, clean, and like-new/resalable &mdash; no material wear, unauthorized modification, missing components, odor, stain, corrosion, misuse, or damage after delivery. All manuals, keys, hardware, cables, consoles, and other included items must come back. Issuing an RA is permission to start the process, not final acceptance &mdash; that happens after receipt, inspection, and cost reconciliation.</p>
  <p>Keep original packaging until you're satisfied with the product; it's normally required for return. If it's unavailable &mdash; including when removed during install or debris-removal service &mdash; we may approve a professional replacement-packaging plan in writing, at your cost.</p>
  <p>Installation doesn't make a final-sale product returnable, and final-sale status survives installation. An otherwise-eligible installed French Fitness or Body-Solid product may still qualify if the request is timely, the product is complete and like-new, packaging is available or an approved replacement plan is in place, you cover all return-side removal/extraction/repackaging/freight costs, and it passes final inspection. Completed service charges remain nonrefundable regardless.</p>

  <h2>Requesting a return, shipping deadline, and return address</h2>
  <p>Contact us in writing within 14 days of delivery for an RA. <strong>Do not ship, tender to a carrier, deliver to a return location, disassemble, or professionally remove anything for return until written RA instructions are issued</strong> &mdash; the RA states the approved return destination, which controls; our general contact address is not an authorized return destination on its own.</p>
  <p>Once approved, ship within 10 calendar days or the RA becomes void (a new request may be denied if the 14-day window has passed or conditions are no longer met). Follow the RA's carrier, packaging, and documentation instructions exactly; mark the RA number as instructed; use a trackable, insured method; keep your tracking number, pickup receipt, and condition photos. Don't ship freight-collect or to an unlisted address.</p>

  <h2>What can't be returned</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Any brand other than eligible new French Fitness or new Body-Solid, including Core Health &amp; Fitness-supplied products;</li>
    <li>Remanufactured, used, or open-box products of any brand;</li>
    <li>Custom, made-to-order, special-order, clearance, &ldquo;as is,&rdquo; or otherwise excluded products identified before purchase;</li>
    <li>Requests made after 14 days, or products not shipped within 10 days of the RA;</li>
    <li>Products returned without authorization or to the wrong destination;</li>
    <li>Products that are incomplete, materially used, modified, abused, improperly installed/disassembled, or no longer resalable;</li>
    <li>Products missing original packaging without an approved replacement plan;</li>
    <li>Products with altered/removed serial numbers or labels; and</li>
    <li>Products without adequate proof of purchase from Fitness Superstore.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Delivery, installation, and similar service charges, plus actual outbound freight, are nonrefundable once performed/incurred &mdash; this doesn't affect rights tied to defective, damaged, incorrect, incomplete, or nonconforming goods.</p>

  <h2>Refund timing</h2>
  <p>After the return is received, we inspect, test if appropriate, and reconcile costs, then confirm acceptance and the final refund. Approved refunds to the original payment method are generally processed within 5&ndash;10 business days and always within legal deadlines &mdash; for a California buyer, within 30 days once those conditions are met. If paid through third-party financing, any required credit memorandum is issued within the legal deadline, including 7 business days under California law where applicable; your bank or financing provider may need additional time to post it. Amounts you paid directly to an approved provider or carrier aren't deducted twice; any tax adjustment is calculated separately.</p>

  <h2>Cancellations</h2>
  <p><strong>Before shipment:</strong> A standard order can generally be canceled before any part ships, without a restocking fee &mdash; unless it's custom/made-to-order/special-order or otherwise noncancelable per terms disclosed before purchase. Once any part ships or is tendered to a carrier, this section no longer applies (see below).</p>
  <p><strong>After shipment/dispatch:</strong> An eligible French Fitness or Body-Solid product follows the voluntary-return terms above (restocking fee, freight, and other deductions apply). A final-sale product has no voluntary cancellation or return right after dispatch, and refusing delivery without authorization doesn't create one &mdash; it may instead trigger redelivery, storage, or reconsignment charges. A cancellation request after dispatch is not itself an approved return and doesn't authorize refusing delivery.</p>
  <p>If Fitness Superstore cancels an order because the product can't be supplied, we'll provide the refund or remedy required by the order terms and law.</p>

  <h2>Which policy applies?</h2>
  <p>The policy and product-specific disclosures shown before purchase control your order; a later policy change doesn't retroactively make an earlier order more restrictive. A written order-specific exception is more favorable and applies only to that order. Where a conflict involves a right that can't lawfully be waived, the law controls.</p>

  <div class="contact-info">
    <h3>Contact Us for Returns</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>TJF Ventures LLC d/b/a Fitness Superstore</strong><br>
      537 Stone Rd. STE F, Benicia, CA 94510<br>
      Phone: <a href="tel:+19252152927">+1-925-215-2927</a><br>
      Email: <a href="mailto:sales@fitnesssuperstore.com">sales@fitnesssuperstore.com</a>
    </p>
    <p>This contact address is not an authorized return destination unless the written RA specifically identifies it as one.</p>
  </div>
</div>

